# Docker build context exclusions for a ./backend build context.
#
# THIS FILE IS STILL INERT for the compose stack, and it always was: Docker
# reads exactly one ignore file, `<context root>/.dockerignore`, and
# docker-compose.yml builds the backend with `context: .` (the repository root)
# because backend/Dockerfile needs backend/ AND frontend/ in the same context.
#
# The exclusions that actually apply to `docker compose build backend` live in
# the ROOT .dockerignore.  Keep this file for the day the backend context
# becomes ./backend (a backend-only image that drops the SPA); it is written
# for that layout and would be applied verbatim at that point.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
*.egg-info
.idea
.vscode
node_modules
# tests and operator scripts are not needed to serve the API
backend/tests
backend/scripts
backend/validation
backend/.dockerignore
backend/Dockerfile
# local uploads, annotated videos and the SQLite database stay on the host
data
# the YOLO checkpoint is downloaded on first use, not baked in
*.pt
frontend
docs
*.md
!README.md
run.bat
run.sh
docker-compose.yml
pyproject.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.editorconfig
CONTRIBUTING.md
